"{\"path\":\"/export-center\",\"title\":\"Export Center · Cinematic AI Video Studio\",\"body\":\"Cinematic AI\\nVIDEO STUDIO\\n\\nOVERVIEW\\n\\nDashboard\\n\\nCREATE\\n\\nCreate Video\\nMy Projects\\n\\nAI STUDIO\\n\\nAI Script Writer\\nAI Video Generator\\nImage Generator\\nThumbnail Generator\\nVoice Studio\\nMusic Studio\\nSound Effects\\nSubtitle Studio\\nAudio Mix\\nShorts Maker\\nSEO Studio\\n\\nBRAND & MEDIA\\n\\nBrand Kit\\nMedia Library\\n\\nSYSTEM\\n\\nExport Center\\nDownloads\\nUsage & Credits\\nSettings\\nP7\\n\\nP7-7a fixture account\\n\\np7a-fixture@cavs.test\\n\\nStudio\\n/\\nExport Center\\nNew video\\nExport Center\\n\\nThe delivery specification for a project — presets, size estimate and the deliverable manifest, all from the export engine — plus every real render and export job on your account. No project's video has been produced on this build and none can be yet: a project holds no source media until a media provider is connected, so its render reaches the encode stage and stops there, naming that missing input. An encoder is installed, and the only files that exist are encodes of a declared synthetic source — labelled synthetic everywhere they appear, with the properties ffprobe measured in them shown beside the values the specification declares.\\n\\nEXPORT & FINISHING\\n\\nno preset applied\\n\\nThe delivery specification for this project: eight presets with the container, video codec, resolution, frame rate, bitrate, audio and loudness numbers and the SDR-or-HDR colour tag each one would carry — all of them the values the export engine declares, none of them invented here. Pick presets, apply them (the choice is stored on the project, and re-applying the same set writes nothing), and read the size ESTIMATE with its formula and units and the deliverable manifest. No file exists: nothing is decoded, encoded, muxed, tone-mapped, uploaded or written — every number below is a specification, and the byte sizes are arithmetic on the stated formula, not measurements of a file.\\n\\nBelow that, the finishing half: the five sidecar deliverables (SRT, WebVTT, chapters, thumbnail, metadata) with an honest content state per slot and a real preview where content exists, and a per-platform publish-readiness matrix where every rule carries a PASS / FAIL / UNKNOWN badge, the rule's own text, its basis and this project's actual value. Both are read-only: they report what the project holds, produce no file and write nothing.\\n\\nPROJECT\\n\\nEXPORT SPECIFICATION FOR\\nThe tide gauge at Ardnish (P7-7a FIXTURE project)\\n\\nproject p7a_fix_project — The tide gauge at Ardnish (P7-7a FIXTURE project)\\n\\nThe preset choice is stored per project (as project metadata) — switching project re-reads its own choice.\\n\\nDURATION FOR THE SIZE ESTIMATE\\n\\nDURATION (SECONDS)\\nEstimate at this duration\\n\\nduration 180 s (3m 00s) · source: scenes — Duration summed from 9 scene duration(s): 180 s.\\n\\nBlank uses the engine's own sources in order: a duration in the request, then the saved editor timeline, then the sum of the scene durations. The engine accepts 1–7200 s (120 min) and refuses anything else rather than estimating it. A duration is printed above only when the read it came from was taken at exactly the duration the next request would carry — otherwise the line says so, instead of printing a number that belongs to a different request.\\n\\nPRESET CATALOGUE (7)\\n\\nnothing selected · applied none\\n16:9\\nyoutube-2160p\\nYouTube 4K (2160p SDR)\\nYouTube long-form\\n3840×2160 · mp4 · H.265/HEVC\\n30 fps · 45,000 kbps (45 Mbps) + 384 kbps\\nAAC-LC 48000 Hz stereo · -14 LUFS · -1 dBTP\\nSDR Rec.709 / BT.1886 / 100 nits\\nestimate ≈ 973.83 MiB (1,021,140,000 bytes)\\n16:9\\nyoutube-2160p-hdr\\nYouTube 4K HDR10 (2160p)\\nYouTube long-form HDR\\n3840×2160 · mp4 · H.265/HEVC\\n30 fps · 56,000 kbps (56 Mbps) + 384 kbps\\nAAC-LC 48000 Hz stereo · -14 LUFS · -1 dBTP\\nHDR Rec.2020 / PQ (SMPTE ST 2084) / 1000 nits · CLL 1000/400\\nestimate ≈ 1.18 GiB (1,268,640,000 bytes)\\n16:9\\nyoutube-1080p\\nYouTube 1080p (FHD SDR)\\nYouTube long-form\\n1920×1080 · mp4 · H.264/AVC\\n30 fps · 8,000 kbps (8 Mbps) + 384 kbps\\nAAC-LC 48000 Hz stereo · -14 LUFS · -1 dBTP\\nSDR Rec.709 / BT.1886 / 100 nits\\nestimate ≈ 179.9 MiB (188,640,000 bytes)\"}"
